### What

- Refactor the `ProductService` to typescript

### Why

- Improve our conversion of the service layer to ts

### Discussion

**Adding an extra generic to `ExtendedFindConfig`** 

I added an extra generic to the `ExtendedFindConfig` type to make the return type more specific depending on what is passed as a selector (cc @adrien2p). To demonstrate this:
```typescript
// src/types/common.ts
export type ExtendedFindConfig<
  TEntity,
  TWhereKeys = TEntity
> = FindConfig<TEntity> & {
  where: Partial<Writable<TWhereKeys>>
  withDeleted?: boolean
  relations?: string[]
}

// src/services/product.ts
class ProductService {
  async retrieveByExternalId(
    externalId: string,
    config: FindProductConfig = {}
  ): Promise<Product> {
    // ...
  
    const { relations, ...query } = buildQuery(
      { external_id: externalId },
      config
    );
  
    query.where.title; // type error. Because we're only selecting based on the external_id, the `where` object will only include the external_id field
  }
}
```

